@c GENERATED UNDO TABLE END

@node Undo Limits
@section Limits

@itemize @bullet
@item
The right-click menu calls a tool's handler directly, as the user's own
action, and is not logged; buffer edits made that way are still in the
buffer's undo list.
@item
An @code{:async} tool is logged when it calls @code{done}; its change
groups span only its synchronous part.
@item
imgedit's undo stack does not say who pushed a step: undoing an agent's
step after an edit in @code{cmacs-imgedit-mode} takes back that edit
instead.
@item
@code{gsurf_navigate} is not stale after a redirect or a followed link;
only a closed view refuses.
@item
@code{screensaver_set_wallpaper} knows the previous wallpaper only when
a tool started it.
@item
A context switch's undo switches back; what the switch opened stays
open.
@item
A tiled gowl window's geometry is the layout's: its undo puts it back in
the tile layer, not at a pixel position.
@end itemize
